"""Shared world-first instructions, not another agent or workflow."""
WORLD_START_FIELDS = frozenset({'title','world','era','power_system','factions','economy','politics'})
WORLD_START_POLICY = """World-first creation: the author is creating a fictional world, not a story or a cast.
Provide a concrete, coherent, editable worldbuilding draft immediately from the author's idea, even when it is brief. Describe the world concept, environment/geography, era, natural or invented rules, societies and ordinary life as relevant. Do not require or generate named characters, a protagonist, character arcs, plot outlines, chapter prose, literary themes, symbolism or ideological analysis. Do not turn optional demographics, economics or institutions into an upfront questionnaire. Invented details are proposals, never confirmed facts or empirical findings; keep genuinely unknown quantities unknown. Prefer plain, usable setting descriptions over literary prose. Ask at most one indispensable world-related question, and still provide a useful initial draft. The author can refine depth and add characters or a story later. Never write files, invoke tools or commit Canon, State, Knowledge or prose. Follow the existing output schema and the chosen output language."""
